    "blast_radius": "Critical",
    "risk_description": "Organization Takeover (Critical)",
    "exploit_path": "A compromised app with organization_administration: write holds Tier 0 control of the entire org security posture. GitHub bundles org rulesets into this scope: an attacker can modify, disable, or delete organization-wide rulesets and strip branch protection across every repository at once. The same grant manages organization-level self-hosted runners, enabling registration of a malicious runner to intercept jobs, harvest secrets, or inject code into builds. It also allows changing default repository permissions (e.g. from Read to Write or Admin), instantly broadening member access org-wide. Member and owner manipulation (invite malicious users, promote to Owner, demote legitimate admins) remains a direct path to lock the org out of source code, secrets, and pipelines.",
    "overlaps_technical_dependency": false,
    "platform_availability": "all",
    "source": "migrate-toxic-combinations CSV"
